WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.334
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.167
You are here! You made it!

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:07.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you for watching!

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.701
Let's get to some news.

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:13.567
Well, guys, the White House just
backed a bipartisan Senate bill

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:17.067
that would give President Biden
the power to ban TikTok.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:18.067
-Ooh.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.467
[ Audience "oohs" ]

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:21.367
Or, as they're calling it
on TikTok,

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.367
the "Trying to Lose
the Election Challenge."

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:25.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:27.167
I wouldn't worry just yet.

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.901
As of now, Biden thinks TikTok
is the clock on "60 Minutes."

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.367
So it's...

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:34.934
Don't worry. To make it up,
Biden promised us

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.767
that he'd give everybody
100 free hours of AOL.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:40.200
So that's good.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.634
[ Applause ]

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.367
[ Cymbals crash ]

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:47.234
Yeah, officials think China
is using TikTok to spy on us.

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:49.434
Then China was like, "Yeah,
well, we had a backup idea,

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:51.667
but you shot it down, so...

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:55.367
how are we supposed to --
how are we...?"

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.200
That's right.
There's a new Senate bill

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.400
that would allow Biden
to ban TikTok.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.234
It's obviously
a very controversial bill,

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.634
and a lot of politicians
are speaking out about it.

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:06.367
For example,
Senator James Lankford said...

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.834
Then Senator Rick Scott said...

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:25.801
And Senator Chuck Grassley
said...

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.400
Then Senator Rand Paul said...

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.434
Then Senator Roger Marshall
said...

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.934
Then President Trump said...

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:58.634
So, Senator Mitch McConnell
said...

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.567
And finally,
Senator James Lankford said...

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.200
That's -- Everyone --

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:14.067
Everyone got their box checked.
Yeah.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.367
Well, everyone's
talking about this.

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:17.968
Tucker Carlson is being
criticized by both parties

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:22.133
for saying that January 6th
was "mostly peaceful."

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.601
That's like if your main
takeaway from Woodstock '99

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:26.300
was that Limp Bizkit
played "Nookie."

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.167
You know what I'm saying?
Like...

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:31.667
Carlson also said that most of
the rioters were "sightseers."

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.767
But usually when sightseers
go to a museum,

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:35.834
they don't try to take a Picasso
home with them.

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:37.167
I'm just saying.

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:40.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.501
Meanwhile,
new legal documents reveal

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:44.133
that right before January 6th,

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:46.734
Tucker Carlson texted a coworker
about Trump

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:50.000
and said,
"I hate him passionately."

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.000
To be fair,
I feel like every friend group

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.667
has a second group text for that
one person they secretly hate.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.501
"What was Jimmy talking about?"

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:00.701
[ Light laughter ]
Listen to this.

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:03.033
We all knew that
Kim Jong-un had a daughter,

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:05.467
but South Korean
intelligence officials said

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:08.634
now they believe Kim Jong-un
has three kids.

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:10.033
-Ooh.
-Yeah, he has three kids.

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:11.767
Eric, Ivanka, and Jong Jr.

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:12.868
-Ooh.

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:14.968
[ Laughter ]
-Hey, this is exciting.

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:17.901
With the huge box-office success
of "Top Gun: Maverick,"

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:21.567
"Avatar: The Way of Water,"
"Cocaine Bear," and "Creed III,"

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.167
insiders believe that movies
are officially back.

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:26.767
-Yeah!
-Yes!

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:29.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:31.300
And you can tell Netflix
may be a little jealous

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.300
based on some of the
notifications that have been

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.901
popping up lately.

00:03:34.901 --> 00:03:37.834
Notifications like...

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:39.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.701
Then I saw this one. It says...

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:47.400
Then there's...

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:52.501
And finally...

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:55.834
They're definitely upset.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:58.501
-Wow.
-They are upset.

00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:00.200
Some more entertainment news.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.067
NBC has ordered
a car-makeover reality show

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:06.033
based on Mattel's
Hot Wheels toys.

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.767
Yep, a Hot Wheels makeover show.

00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:09.334
People will say, "Whoa.
Look at the cool flames

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:11.767
on the side of that Tesla.
Wait. Those are real.

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:14.467
Hey! You okay?"

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:17.334
Speaking of Tesla,
the U.S. is investigating Tesla

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:20.200
over reports of steering wheels
falling off

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.834
while the cars are being driven.

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:23.167
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.501
I guess that's one way
to make a car driverless.

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:26.667
Uh...

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:28.567
Take the steering wheel off.

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:31.868
Well, get this. A viral TikTok
revealed that Chuck E. Cheese

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:35.400
still uses floppy disks
for its animatronic band.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.133
[ Audience groans ]
Yeah.

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:39.701
Well, anyway, to prove that
they're still cool and modern,

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:42.033
Chuck E. Cheese updated
some of the band's music.

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:44.033
And it's a little surprising.
Take a look at this.

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:47.067
-♪ Mummy don't know
daddy's getting hot ♪

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:50.667
♪ At the body shop
doing something unholy ♪

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:52.901
I just thought that was --
Yeah, that was interesting.

00:04:52.901 --> 00:04:55.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
I don't know.

00:04:55.968 --> 00:04:58.434
Did you guys see this?

00:04:58.434 --> 00:05:03.067
More than 300 people just got
sick on a Princess cruise ship.

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:06.267
Meanwhile, Carnival was like,
"300? That is so last year."

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:08.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.601 --> 00:05:10.667
Source of the outbreak
hasn't been confirmed,

00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:13.000
but when the news broke,
the sushi buffet

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.467
grew legs and moonwalked
out of the room.

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:18.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:21.267
Hey, I saw a new survey
that said the top reasons

00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:24.200
guests would leave a hotel room
they already paid for are...

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:27.534
bed bugs, a bad smell,
and finding a camera.

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:30.133
[ Audience groans ]
Motel 6 heard it and was like,

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.801
"Hey! 3 for 3!
We got hotel bingo! Alright!

00:05:32.801 --> 00:05:34.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:36.534
Cool."

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:38.167
And, finally,
have you guys noticed

00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:40.200
that when you start typing
something on Google,

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.534
it automatically tries to
complete the search for you?

00:05:42.534 --> 00:05:44.567
Yeah, well, it autofills
what you're looking for,

00:05:44.567 --> 00:05:46.567
but sometimes their suggestions
are a little off.

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:47.834
I'm gonna show you what I mean.

00:05:47.834 --> 00:05:49.167
It's time for
"Google Autofails."

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:50.601
Here. Check this out.

00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:55.067
-♪ Google Autofails, yeah ♪

00:05:55.067 --> 00:05:56.934
-Here's an example
that I typed in.

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:58.934
I said,
"Which country should I..."

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:00.133
These three things pop up.

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:01.934
"...visit for Spring Break?"

00:06:01.934 --> 00:06:03.334
"...check out in Europe?"

00:06:03.334 --> 00:06:05.434
"...move to after the U.S.
bans TikTok?"

00:06:05.434 --> 00:06:06.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:08.434
These are autofills.
-Autofails!

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.434
Here's another one I typed in.

00:06:10.434 --> 00:06:12.100
It said,
"Why did Tucker Carlson..."

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.801
It said,
"...get his own show?"

00:06:13.801 --> 00:06:15.534
"...get the January 6th tapes?"

00:06:15.534 --> 00:06:17.734
"...describe 'Creed III'
as 'mostly peaceful'?"

00:06:17.734 --> 00:06:20.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.868 --> 00:06:22.701
Next up, I typed in,

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:24.634
"Are the contestants on
'The Masked Singer"..."

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:26.467
It said, "...really singing?"

00:06:26.467 --> 00:06:27.968
"...getting paid?"

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:29.334
"...volunteers or prisoners?"

00:06:29.334 --> 00:06:33.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.367 --> 00:06:35.868
Next up, I typed in,
"Can H&amp;R Block..."

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:37.667
It said, "...do my taxes?"

00:06:37.667 --> 00:06:39.100
"...answer my questions?"

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.968
"...take a shoebox full
of loose documents

00:06:40.968 --> 00:06:42.234
and make sure
I don't go to prison?"

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:44.067
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.067 --> 00:06:45.601
"Look at this. Help me."

00:06:45.601 --> 00:06:49.267
And finally, I typed in,
"I feel out of control when..."

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:51.133
It said, "...I party too much."

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:52.601
"...I have too much work."

00:06:52.601 --> 00:06:54.634
"...the steering wheel
on my Tesla falls off."

00:06:54.634 --> 00:06:56.467
That's it for
"Google Autofails."

